1
00:06:03,529 --> 00:06:09,529
Welcome back to where the magic began.

2
00:12:07,058 --> 00:12:13,058
Harry Potter 20th Anniversary: Return to Hogwarts is a
documentary film directed by Joe Pearlman.

3
00:18:10,588 --> 00:18:16,588
An enchanting making-of story told through all-new in-depth interviews and cast conversations, inviting fans
on a magical first-person journey through one of the most beloved film franchises of all time.

4
00:24:14,117 --> 00:24:20,117
Self, played by Daniel Radcliffe.

5
00:30:17,647 --> 00:30:23,647
Self, played by Rupert Grint.

6
00:36:21,176 --> 00:36:27,176
Self, played by Emma Watson.

7
00:42:24,705 --> 00:42:30,705
Self, played by Bonnie Wright.

8
00:48:28,235 --> 00:48:34,235
Self, played by Matthew Lewis.

9
00:54:31,764 --> 00:54:37,764
Self, played by Tom Felton.

10
01:00:35,294 --> 01:00:41,294
Harry Potter 20th Anniversary: Return to Hogwarts is a television
special released on 1 January 2022 on HBO Max.

11
01:06:38,823 --> 01:06:44,823
It is a reunion special for the cast and crew of the Harry Potter film series, marking the
twentieth anniversary of the series' first instalment, The Philosopher's Stone.

12
01:12:42,352 --> 01:12:48,352
It was produced by Warner Bros.

13
01:18:45,882 --> 01:18:51,882
Unscripted Television in association with Warner Horizon
and executive produced by Casey Patterson.

14
01:24:49,411 --> 01:24:55,411
The films' protagonist trio Daniel Radcliffe, Rupert Grint, and Emma Watson appear throughout the special, along with surviving principal cast members Helena Bonham Carter, Robbie Coltrane, Ralph Fiennes, Jason Isaacs, Gary Oldman, Tom Felton,
James Phelps, Oliver Phelps, Mark Williams, Bonnie Wright, Alfred Enoch, Ian Hart, Toby Jones, Matthew Lewis, and Evanna Lynch, producer David Heyman, and filmmakers Chris Columbus, Alfonso Cuarón, Mike Newell, and David Yates.

15
01:30:52,941 --> 01:30:58,941
The special is also notable for marking Coltrane's final on-screen
appearance prior to his death on 14 October 2022.

16
01:36:56,470 --> 01:37:02,470
The film explores themes of reunion, fantasy world, social
gathering, college reunion, cinema history.
